From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 00:24:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] asahi: widen 16-bit varyings before st_vary

UVS slots are 32-bit: st_vary only takes 32-bit sources, and the fragment
shader reads varyings as 32-bit values and converts them after
interpolation (agx_nir_lower_interpolation). A 16-bit vertex output, such
as a half varying from SPIR-V Float16 (Metal shaders translated to
SPIR-V), reached st_vary as a 16-bit source, and the backend aborted the
process that compiled the pipeline (value.size == AGX_SIZE_32).

Widen 16-bit outputs to 32 bits by their type before st_vary: f2f32 for
floats, i2i32 for signed and u2u32 for other integers.

Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/src/asahi/lib/agx_nir_lower_uvs.c b/src/asahi/lib/agx_nir_lower_uvs.c
index 75d3c0d..ce6b9b1 100644
--- a/src/asahi/lib/agx_nir_lower_uvs.c
+++ b/src/asahi/lib/agx_nir_lower_uvs.c
@@ -64,6 +64,25 @@ lower(nir_builder *b, nir_intrinsic_instr *intr, void *data)
    nir_def *value = intr->src[0].ssa;
    nir_def *offset = intr->src[1].ssa;
 
+   /* UVS slots are 32-bit (st_vary only takes 32-bit sources), and the
+    * fragment shader reads varyings as 32-bit and converts after
+    * interpolation (agx_nir_lower_interpolation). Widen 16-bit outputs
+    * (e.g. half varyings from SPIR-V Float16) according to their type.
+    */
+   if (value->bit_size == 16) {
+      switch (nir_alu_type_get_base_type(nir_intrinsic_src_type(intr))) {
+      case nir_type_float:
+         value = nir_f2f32(b, value);
+         break;
+      case nir_type_int:
+         value = nir_i2i32(b, value);
+         break;
+      default:
+         value = nir_u2u32(b, value);
+         break;
+      }
+   }
+
    /* If there is only 1 user varying, it is at the base of the varying section.
     * This saves us an indirection on simple separate shaders.
     */
